courses.learning_outcomes:
Upon the successful completion of this course, student will be able:
1. To understand the basic model of training and development, and its role in hospitality and real estate organizations;
2. To acquire basic skills in analyzing the needs, designing, delivering and evaluating various training and development activities;
3. To design training interventions using a variety of training methodologies;
4. To learn how to deliver a training session;
5. To acquire skills to evaluate the effectiveness of training interventions;

courses.course_syllabus:
This course is designed to facilitate students’ understanding of the frameworks and conceptual underpinnings of learning, training & development (T&D), and their application of the latest HRD tools and techniques in addressing learning and development issues. The course will also help in developing the thinking on how HRD/T&D can play significant roles in delivering competitive advantage for organization.
After completion of this course, students should be able
1. To clearly understand the conceptual underpinnings of T&D and gain knowledge of the entire T&D framework and processes from needs assessments to its design, implementation and evaluation;
2. To develop critical thinking/creativity and problem solving & decision-making ability as they analyze & conduct evaluations and design T&D solutions in business simulated case-studies and exercises;
3. To develop team and collaborative skills as they work in groups in the class assignments/exercises.

courses.learning_outcomes:
Upon the successful completion of this course, student will be able:
1. To identify different research methods and their theoretical underpinnings;
2. To demonstrate an ability to identify, analyze and synthesize literature related to a research question;
3. To critically analyze and demonstrate an ability to formulate viable research questions;
4. To demonstrate an understanding and ability to undertake the range of tasks necessary to completing a research project;
5. To identify and engage with the range of ethical issues involved in the conduct of a research project.

courses.course_syllabus:
This course offers an overview of research methodology including basic concepts employed in quantitative and qualitative research methods.
After completion of this course, students should be able
1. To demonstrate knowledge of research process;
2. To compare and contrast quantitative and qualitative research;
3. To demonstrate skills in using online data bases and software;
4. To describe, compare, and contrast descriptive and inferential statistics;
5. To describe sampling methods, measurement scales and instruments, and appropriate uses of each.

courses.learning_outcomes:
Upon the completion of the study trip, students are expected to
1. understand key aspects of the natural, economic, social, and cultural environments of the destination;
2. understand key aspects of operations/strategies of local hospitality/tourism organizations;
3. develop a better understanding of the impacts of the hospitality/tourism industry;
4. increase their ability to communicate with and learn from people from different cultural backgrounds;
5. increase their ability to reflect on personal experiences and values.

