courses.learning_outcomes:
Upon completion of the course, the students should be able to:
• Be familiar with major perspectives on strategic management and their applications in hospitality businesses;
• Identify critical elements of a hospitality organization's external environment and its internal resource base;
• Understand generic business and corporate strategies and how to choose appropriate strategy(ies) that meet environmental requirements and match organizational resources / capabilities;
• Apply knowledge previously acquired from work experience and the classroom to strategic issues related to hospitality companies; and
• Develop and exercise critical thinking, persuasive written and verbal communication skills.

Upon completion of this course, students should be able to:
• Understand the land tenure system in Hong Kong and apply the knowledge of land use control in real estate settings in a global context;
• Know the two dimensional development control: lease control and statutory control in Hong Kong, the role of various authorities in the land development control;
• Understand and apply town planning, land control and development knowledge to delivering excellent services to potential clients;
• Develop creative thinking and problem solving skills relevant to land development issues;
• Develop self-managed ability, leadership skills, team work spirit, analytical and communicative skills and oral presentation skills that are appropriate in a variety of investment scenarios through case studies and group projects;
• Identify and address ethical issues in both land investment and development settings.

At the conclusion of the course, students are expected to be able to:
1. Identify the main types of risk confronted by financial institutions;
2. Apply relevant techniques to measure and manage those risks;
3. Understand the main regulations and operations of financial institutions within such regulations;
4. Engage in informed discussion of some of the contemporary issues in a local and international context, affecting financial institutions and their owners, managers, employees and customers;
5. Understand key banking practices in risk management as relevant to real estate assets and investments;
6. Work collaboratively to complete a task.
